          "sourceDoi": "10.1103/physreve.91.062144",
          "targetDoi": "10.1073/pnas.0506347102",
          "snippet": "Our approach is based on the observation that systems governed by linear forces can be mapped to a generalization of the Ornstein-Uhlenbeck process, for which a general solution is known [19]. For nonlinear forces, a common approach is to solve the system using perturbation theory [20].",
