          "targetDoi": "10.1016/s0006-3495(92)81860-x",
          "snippet": "Engine realizations hitherto [1,2] assumed that the optical forces exerted on the microsphere are conservative and the surrounding medium acts as a thermal bath. In principle, however, non-conservative forces are also exerted on the colloidal particle due to light scattering at the microsphere-water interface [8][9][10][11][12]. The resulting circulations in the probability flux termed -Brownian vortexes -could locally drive the bath out of equilibrium.",
          "type": "mentioning"
